                <pb facs="0339" n="331" sameAs="frus:frus1937v04/pg331"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">393.1115/867: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Japan</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Grew</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Tokyo</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-09-16T18:00:00+09:00">September 16, 1937—6
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received September 16—7:52 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>378. Following telegram has been sent to Shanghai: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“September 16, 5 p.m. Your 703, September 14, 3 p.m., to the
                                Department.<anchor n="35" xml:id="d369-f1"/> Evacuation from
                            Mokanshan. Following memorandum has been received today from the Foreign
                            Office: <quote rend="blockquote">
                                <p>‘The Imperial Government has completed necessary arrangements to
                                    safeguard about 150 American nationals now at Mokanshan near
                                    Hangchow, Chekiang Province, who will leave overland for Ningpo
                                    on September 22 and are due to arrive at Shanghai on September
                                    23 on the British steamer <hi rendition="#italic">Hsin
                                        Peking</hi>’.</p>
                            </quote></p>
                        <p>Repeated to Department.”</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Grew</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
